{"metadata":{"title":"KsfParams","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KsfParams"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK9KsfParamsV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KsfParams"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KsfParams"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cost properties are optional on purpose: they arrive flat, and a field that does not apply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the named function is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent, not zero"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Reading a missing "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stretch at the wrong cost and fail against a record that is perfectly good (§23.4 rule 5)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These are never cached across exchanges and never defaulted locally. A credential enrolled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under one cost keeps working after a tenant raises its policy, so a client that guessed would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"derive a different randomized password and report “invalid password” for one that is entirely","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"correct (§23.4 rule 2).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"This is where Swift stopped needing a `pbkdf2_sha256`